(6590428, 982501, 86447, '<td valign="top">Ha!   This made me snort!  LOL!  Too cute.</td>', 'Ha!   This made me snort!  LOL!  Too cute.', '2011-11-09 09:07:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590429, 983061, 86447, '<td valign="top">Wow.   Perfection of challenge topic has been reached.   Well done!</td>', 'Wow.   Perfection of challenge topic has been reached.   Well done!', '2011-11-09 09:08:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590431, 983017, 86447, '<td valign="top">Oh!  Well done!</td>', 'Oh!  Well done!', '2011-11-09 09:09:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590433, 983080, 86447, '<td valign="top">Ha!    Too cute!</td>', 'Ha!    Too cute!', '2011-11-09 09:10:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590435, 983112, 86447, '<td valign="top">Molly is ADORABLE.  And well-photographed.</td>', 'Molly is ADORABLE.  And well-photographed.', '2011-11-09 09:12:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590442, 983123, 54446, '<td valign="top">I see the effort to compose correctly with golden ratio in mind.  Good job!  However....it is not visually balanced because of the shape of the rectangle.   I didn''t mark this lower because of the rectangle proportions of 1:1.4.  Use of the golden ratio composition is best with use of a 1:1.618 rectangle.... sometimes called a golden rectangle.  While you may not believe me, you would have a fantastic, more visually balanced image with an 800x495 rectangle.  Hey, it''s not an easy crop because it''s longer (or taller) than rectangles to which we are accustomed.  You''ve already clipped the feet, so a longer rectangle might have mitigated that distraction by directing the eye to that beautiful face.  (Same problem with my entry.)</td>', 'I see the effort to compose correctly with golden ratio in mind.  Good job!  However....it is not visually balanced because of the shape of the rectangle.   I didn''t mark this lower because of the rectangle proportions of 1:1.4.  Use of the golden ratio composition is best with use of a 1:1.618 rectangle.... sometimes called a golden rectangle.  While you may not believe me, you would have a fantastic, more visually balanced image with an 800x495 rectangle.  Hey, it''s not an easy crop because it''s longer (or taller) than rectangles to which we are accustomed.  You''ve already clipped the feet, so a longer rectangle might have mitigated that distraction by directing the eye to that beautiful face.  (Same problem with my entry.)', '2011-11-09 09:26:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590470, 983056, 54446, '<td valign="top">Wow, right idea.  But, the rectangle is too long.  Had you cropped 75 pixels off the right side, you would have had a very visually balanced image.  I didn''t mark down for not have a golden rectangle.  Still a fine image with interesting lighting and stacked hills.  8</td>', 'Wow, right idea.  But, the rectangle is too long.  Had you cropped 75 pixels off the right side, you would have had a very visually balanced image.  I didn''t mark down for not have a golden rectangle.  Still a fine image with interesting lighting and stacked hills.  8', '2011-11-09 10:09:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6590492, 982183, 113278, '<td valign="top">Completely brilliant.</td>', 'Completely brilliant.', '2011-11-09 10:56:06.000000', NULL, 1),
