(6591026, 983105, 136989, '<td valign="top">Love the composition and details.  The white is a bit harsh but that could be my monitor.  Not sure on that.</td>', 'Love the composition and details.  The white is a bit harsh but that could be my monitor.  Not sure on that.', '2011-11-09 20:45:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591027, 983135, 136989, '<td valign="top">Terrific colors and composition.  I need those shoes!</td>', 'Terrific colors and composition.  I need those shoes!', '2011-11-09 20:46:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591028, 983147, 136989, '<td valign="top">Sorry not feeling the green...</td>', 'Sorry not feeling the green...', '2011-11-09 20:47:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591029, 983080, 136989, '<td valign="top">LOL  Too funny.  Nicely done.</td>', 'LOL  Too funny.  Nicely done.', '2011-11-09 20:48:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591038, 982383, 136989, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.  A great fall portrait in natural colors/light.</td>', 'Beautiful.  A great fall portrait in natural colors/light.', '2011-11-09 21:01:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591041, 982584, 136989, '<td valign="top">Great colors and details.  I know the cupola (?) was placed for the challenge but the ground is a bit less interesting than a tad more sky would have been.</td>', 'Great colors and details.  I know the cupola (?) was placed for the challenge but the ground is a bit less interesting than a tad more sky would have been.', '2011-11-09 21:02:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591042, 983079, 136989, '<td valign="top">Who would have thought that hanging from the ceiling could look so elegant?  Love it.</td>', 'Who would have thought that hanging from the ceiling could look so elegant?  Love it.', '2011-11-09 21:03:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591044, 982738, 94265, '<td valign="top">I love the focus and perspective on this one, very nice shot luv. :-)</td>', 'I love the focus and perspective on this one, very nice shot luv. :-)', '2011-11-09 21:04:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591045, 983111, 136989, '<td valign="top">Sorry ... I can''t tell what I am looking at. :(</td>', 'Sorry ... I can''t tell what I am looking at. :(', '2011-11-09 21:05:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591047, 983144, 94265, '<td valign="top">Lovely and sharp focus on the cheetah, beautiful animal, nice shot. The green saturation is maybe up a little high for my taste though, that grass off to the right keeps trying to drag my eye away from the kitty.</td>', 'Lovely and sharp focus on the cheetah, beautiful animal, nice shot. The green saturation is maybe up a little high for my taste though, that grass off to the right keeps trying to drag my eye away from the kitty.', '2011-11-09 21:06:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591052, 983123, 15711, '<td valign="top">What a cutie.  This would make an adorable holiday card.</td>', 'What a cutie.  This would make an adorable holiday card.', '2011-11-09 21:13:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591055, 982978, 15711, '<td valign="top">Oh my.  I love the ethereal quality.  Divine bokeh.  My fav so far.</td>', 'Oh my.  I love the ethereal quality.  Divine bokeh.  My fav so far.', '2011-11-09 21:14:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591062, 983112, 15711, '<td valign="top">What a muffin!!!!!!!  I miss puppy breath.</td>', 'What a muffin!!!!!!!  I miss puppy breath.', '2011-11-09 21:19:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591063, 983105, 15711, '<td valign="top">Lovely stark contrasts.</td>', 'Lovely stark contrasts.', '2011-11-09 21:19:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591065, 982922, 15711, '<td valign="top">Oh my@@@@@@</td>', 'Oh my@@@@@@', '2011-11-09 21:21:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591068, 982183, 15711, '<td valign="top">That is magnificent.  Since I don''t know how to vote on that weird golden rule, I''m just going to go on my gut because this is just brilliant.</td>', 'That is magnificent.  Since I don''t know how to vote on that weird golden rule, I''m just going to go on my gut because this is just brilliant.', '2011-11-09 21:22:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591070, 982996, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is wonderful.</td>', 'This is wonderful.', '2011-11-09 21:22:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591071, 983063, 15711, '<td valign="top">I love her cocked head. &gt;^^&lt;</td>', 'I love her cocked head. >^^<', '2011-11-09 21:23:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591073, 983152, 15711, '<td valign="top">This is really beautifully captured.</td>', 'This is really beautifully captured.', '2011-11-09 21:23:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591074, 982678, 30861, '<td valign="top">Mr Minso, are you all RIGHT?</td>', 'Mr Minso, are you all RIGHT?', '2011-11-09 21:23:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591075, 983081, 15711, '<td valign="top">Oh I just love this.  I shouldn''t be affected by titles, but I am.  9 from me.</td>', 'Oh I just love this.  I shouldn''t be affected by titles, but I am.  9 from me.', '2011-11-09 21:24:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591148, 982947, 100831, '<td valign="top">The light and tones are spectacular.</td>', 'The light and tones are spectacular.', '2011-11-09 22:33:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591153, 983129, 100831, '<td valign="top">The darks and rich colors and just stunning. And the composition is terrific... the way the faces are turned. The light. Love this.</td>', 'The darks and rich colors and just stunning. And the composition is terrific... the way the faces are turned. The light. Love this.', '2011-11-09 22:38:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591204, 983069, 114285, '<td valign="top">Pretty cool effect you have here, but i feel the main problem is that there is no real  focal point. Well not that I can see, I could be wrong, I don''t see what you saw.</td>', 'Pretty cool effect you have here, but i feel the main problem is that there is no real  focal point. Well not that I can see, I could be wrong, I don''t see what you saw.', '2011-11-10 00:11:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591205, 982978, 114285, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot.</td>', 'Lovely shot.', '2011-11-10 00:11:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591206, 982970, 114285, '<td valign="top">Love the way you processed this, I''ll have to try that one day.</td>', 'Love the way you processed this, I''ll have to try that one day.', '2011-11-10 00:12:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591268, 983079, 119771, '<td valign="top">beautiful picture, good lighting, charming woman !</td>', 'beautiful picture, good lighting, charming woman !', '2011-11-10 03:42:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591275, 981929, 56502, '<td valign="top">My idea on tilt is you either make it clear that it is intentional, or you make sure horizontal and vertical lines are pretty much correct. This tilt does not look really intentional to me.</td>', 'My idea on tilt is you either make it clear that it is intentional, or you make sure horizontal and vertical lines are pretty much correct. This tilt does not look really intentional to me.', '2011-11-10 05:00:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591306, 983080, 114969, '<td valign="top">I love this one :-) Very fun and creative. My only concern is... why not use a golden ratio crop? Would have been perfect. Very good nonetheless!</td>', 'I love this one :-) Very fun and creative. My only concern is... why not use a golden ratio crop? Would have been perfect. Very good nonetheless!', '2011-11-10 06:59:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591307, 983089, 114969, '<td valign="top">Very good photo, there is a very nice feel to it: simple, joyful, charmful! Also, it perfectly fits the challenge: the crop and composition are perfect. The depth of field also works great here, and leads even more to the focus point (not that it was needed anyway :-)). Great job!</td>', 'Very good photo, there is a very nice feel to it: simple, joyful, charmful! Also, it perfectly fits the challenge: the crop and composition are perfect. The depth of field also works great here, and leads even more to the focus point (not that it was needed anyway :-)). Great job!', '2011-11-10 06:59:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591308, 982678, 114969, '<td valign="top">That one is very good. The depth of field really adds here, and the composition absolutely fits the challenge (one of the few!). I obviously also love the creativity!</td>', 'That one is very good. The depth of field really adds here, and the composition absolutely fits the challenge (one of the few!). I obviously also love the creativity!', '2011-11-10 06:59:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591309, 982678, 118154, '<td valign="top">Iv,e seen that cheeky little face before. Neat idea,good timing too.</td>', 'Iv,e seen that cheeky little face before. Neat idea,good timing too.', '2011-11-10 06:59:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591310, 983129, 114969, '<td valign="top">I really like that photo. The crop is golden, in every sense of the word. Moreover, the blur really works well here, and the tones are perfect for rendering this mood. The mother in the darkness is fabulous, as well as the child''s expression. My only concern would be about the colored noise: it''s a little bit disturbing, I think I would have preferred a monochromatic noise instead, but I''m nitpicking. Again, great photo, and a perfect illustration of the challenge.</td>', 'I really like that photo. The crop is golden, in every sense of the word. Moreover, the blur really works well here, and the tones are perfect for rendering this mood. The mother in the darkness is fabulous, as well as the child''s expression. My only concern would be about the colored noise: it''s a little bit disturbing, I think I would have preferred a monochromatic noise instead, but I''m nitpicking. Again, great photo, and a perfect illustration of the challenge.', '2011-11-10 07:00:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591311, 982944, 118154, '<td valign="top">great lighting and crop ,even though the eyes are dark this is one of my front pagers.</td>', 'great lighting and crop ,even though the eyes are dark this is one of my front pagers.', '2011-11-10 07:01:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591312, 983123, 118154, '<td valign="top">Another nice image from a winning photographer,should go well.</td>', 'Another nice image from a winning photographer,should go well.', '2011-11-10 07:03:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591313, 982183, 118154, '<td valign="top">Like this image very much,front page for me.</td>', 'Like this image very much,front page for me.', '2011-11-10 07:03:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591323, 983069, 113278, '<td valign="top">Per your request. I think you managed to meet the challenge by finding a unique natural formation which is definitely cool. But it was not photographed in a unique way and it really looks like a snap shot. The lighting is very flat but I think the biggest downfall is that it is just too busy. The ice formation is interesting but you lose much impact with all of the leaves and branches/twigs everywhere. I think if you could have kept the ice but physically removed much of the distracting elements that would help. The colors are very boring, its ice and rock so not much you can do about that but I contrasty black and white conversion would make it more interesting. Don''t be disheartened, many of us start here just learning our ways, just look at some of my first entries. I hope this helped some, if you have any other questions feel free to PM me.</td>', 'Per your request. I think you managed to meet the challenge by finding a unique natural formation which is definitely cool. But it was not photographed in a unique way and it really looks like a snap shot. The lighting is very flat but I think the biggest downfall is that it is just too busy. The ice formation is interesting but you lose much impact with all of the leaves and branches/twigs everywhere. I think if you could have kept the ice but physically removed much of the distracting elements that would help. The colors are very boring, its ice and rock so not much you can do about that but I contrasty black and white conversion would make it more interesting. Don''t be disheartened, many of us start here just learning our ways, just look at some of my first entries. I hope this helped some, if you have any other questions feel free to PM me.', '2011-11-10 07:28:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591329, 983105, 94265, '<td valign="top">Very pretty bird, I''m curious as to how you got a background behind her that looks like a studio, lol. Lovely shot.</td>', 'Very pretty bird, I''m curious as to how you got a background behind her that looks like a studio, lol. Lovely shot.', '2011-11-10 07:35:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591330, 983112, 94265, '<td valign="top">I like her straight-on contact with the camera, lovely little dog.</td>', 'I like her straight-on contact with the camera, lovely little dog.', '2011-11-10 07:36:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591331, 983051, 94265, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot; some nicely lit reflections, cool shapes, great DOF and good crisp sharpness on the main spiral. Good job.</td>', 'I really like this shot; some nicely lit reflections, cool shapes, great DOF and good crisp sharpness on the main spiral. Good job.', '2011-11-10 07:37:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591332, 983041, 94265, '<td valign="top">I like this, the title works well both as an obvious choice and also because where the leaf is caught in the fence seems to match up with the Fibonacci spiral focal point, if I''ve got that right! Nice muted colour in the bokeh too, makes the red stand out more.</td>', 'I like this, the title works well both as an obvious choice and also because where the leaf is caught in the fence seems to match up with the Fibonacci spiral focal point, if I''ve got that right! Nice muted colour in the bokeh too, makes the red stand out more.', '2011-11-10 07:38:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591416, 982501, 54446, '<td valign="top">Not quite on target, but close.</td>', 'Not quite on target, but close.', '2011-11-10 11:10:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591438, 983079, 118154, '<td valign="top">Looks very much like a french production to me. Lovely lighting and everything else. Hope to see this near the top.</td>', 'Looks very much like a french production to me. Lovely lighting and everything else. Hope to see this near the top.', '2011-11-10 12:07:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591439, 983089, 118154, '<td valign="top">Has a real natural look to it,don,t think iv''e ever seen anything like this on a Sunday morning.<br/>Anyway its a nice shot and works very well,hope to see it on the front page.</td>', 'Has a real natural look to it,don,t think iv''e ever seen anything like this on a Sunday morning.Anyway its a nice shot and works very well,hope to see it on the front page.', '2011-11-10 12:11:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591458, 982819, 16046, '<td valign="top">Best in show, outstanding image!</td>', 'Best in show, outstanding image!', '2011-11-10 12:38:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591539, 983047, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea, perhaps more of a melody of color than a symphony, given the prevalent hue. I am not necessarily a manic with focus when soften serves a purpose, however in this case I find that the out of focus at the extremities of the flower detracts for the image, particularly because the blur is very digital in look. Perhaps, a bit more depth of field, if achievable, would have improved the image. I am not 100% sure this framing actually works. Possibly, having lines and flower to curve back into the frame would have helped.</td>', 'Interesting idea, perhaps more of a melody of color than a symphony, given the prevalent hue. I am not necessarily a manic with focus when soften serves a purpose, however in this case I find that the out of focus at the extremities of the flower detracts for the image, particularly because the blur is very digital in look. Perhaps, a bit more depth of field, if achievable, would have improved the image. I am not 100% sure this framing actually works. Possibly, having lines and flower to curve back into the frame would have helped.', '2011-11-10 14:37:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591576, 982738, 49018, '<td valign="top">Repetitive patterns are often interesting, but in this case I find the alignment of the benches and perspective compression work against stressing the pattern. I personally find the misalignment of the benches to be somewhat attractive, like a disconnected path, but I do not find the image particularly strong.  I wonder if it might have worked better by including more of the road vanishing in the distance, possibly including an approaching figure suggesting someone will eventually sit.</td>', 'Repetitive patterns are often interesting, but in this case I find the alignment of the benches and perspective compression work against stressing the pattern. I personally find the misalignment of the benches to be somewhat attractive, like a disconnected path, but I do not find the image particularly strong.  I wonder if it might have worked better by including more of the road vanishing in the distance, possibly including an approaching figure suggesting someone will eventually sit.', '2011-11-10 15:14:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591603, 983073, 10848, '<td valign="top">Outstanding image, love the lighting.</td>', 'Outstanding image, love the lighting.', '2011-11-10 16:01:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591604, 983113, 10848, '<td valign="top">Outstanding!!</td>', 'Outstanding!!', '2011-11-10 16:04:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591605, 983080, 10848, '<td valign="top">Very creative!</td>', 'Very creative!', '2011-11-10 16:05:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591609, 983037, 10848, '<td valign="top">Great image!</td>', 'Great image!', '2011-11-10 16:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591611, 983061, 10848, '<td valign="top">Very nice!</td>', 'Very nice!', '2011-11-10 16:16:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591632, 983059, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting texture and composition. A bit more detail in the highlights and definitely more brightness in the sky would have made for a better image, in my opinion.</td>', 'Interesting texture and composition. A bit more detail in the highlights and definitely more brightness in the sky would have made for a better image, in my opinion.', '2011-11-10 16:45:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591657, 982839, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea. I like the sense of movement and the speckles of ice cream but I think it would have worked better with the bat (cricket? croquet? uhh) more blurred and leaving a trail (slow shutter speed and flash perhaps?). This way, also because the left side of the bat is in focus and the ice cream is on the right side, it gives me the weird feeling that the bat is swinging back towards the left. Independently from the subject of the challenge, cropping so to leave more space on the right (for the ice cream to fly) would have made for a more effective image, in my opinion. Including a two hands grip and a bit of the forearms would have also made the blow look more forceful (poor icecream :)</td>', 'Interesting idea. I like the sense of movement and the speckles of ice cream but I think it would have worked better with the bat (cricket? croquet? uhh) more blurred and leaving a trail (slow shutter speed and flash perhaps?). This way, also because the left side of the bat is in focus and the ice cream is on the right side, it gives me the weird feeling that the bat is swinging back towards the left. Independently from the subject of the challenge, cropping so to leave more space on the right (for the ice cream to fly) would have made for a more effective image, in my opinion. Including a two hands grip and a bit of the forearms would have also made the blow look more forceful (poor icecream :)', '2011-11-10 17:19:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591665, 983069, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice and a rare find. I wonder if a more angular lighting could have made for a more dramatic image, possibly underexposing a bit to keep more texture in the ice. Also, while I guess that in a large print this would be less of a problem, at this resolution a more out of focus background would have helped a lot defining the spiral further. Very interesting image.</td>', 'Nice and a rare find. I wonder if a more angular lighting could have made for a more dramatic image, possibly underexposing a bit to keep more texture in the ice. Also, while I guess that in a large print this would be less of a problem, at this resolution a more out of focus background would have helped a lot defining the spiral further. Very interesting image.', '2011-11-10 17:27:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591667, 982432, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice autumn colours. Is she wondering at the falling leaves? The colours on jackets and trousers lack of details and look a bit unnatural, maybe a bit of of underexposure to receover in postprocessing could have helped in that and also in preserving detail in the highlights. The white cloth on the wall is a bit distracting.</td>', 'Nice autumn colours. Is she wondering at the falling leaves? The colours on jackets and trousers lack of details and look a bit unnatural, maybe a bit of of underexposure to receover in postprocessing could have helped in that and also in preserving detail in the highlights. The white cloth on the wall is a bit distracting.', '2011-11-10 17:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591670, 982978, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice bokeh. As the focal point of the spiral is on the bottom left leaf, and the shot plays on leaves definition versus extreme bokeh, a slightly different angle to exclude the out of focus twig on the left would have worked better for me.</td>', 'Nice bokeh. As the focal point of the spiral is on the bottom left leaf, and the shot plays on leaves definition versus extreme bokeh, a slightly different angle to exclude the out of focus twig on the left would have worked better for me.', '2011-11-10 17:37:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591672, 982852, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting, I like the negative blue space and the red attire certanly gives presence to the axe man. A closer crop, resolution permitting, might have served the golden ratio principle better. Also, but really this is my personal opinion, I kind of prefer this kind of shots to be either more blurred for the movement or tack sharp (possibly with drops of sweat frozen mid air, ok, that''s probably asking too much).</td>', 'Interesting, I like the negative blue space and the red attire certanly gives presence to the axe man. A closer crop, resolution permitting, might have served the golden ratio principle better. Also, but really this is my personal opinion, I kind of prefer this kind of shots to be either more blurred for the movement or tack sharp (possibly with drops of sweat frozen mid air, ok, that''s probably asking too much).', '2011-11-10 17:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591675, 982176, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like it. While the blown highlights certainly contribute to the ''sunny day'' feeling, a bit more detail in the leaves would have been pleasant. If the dark border on the left side would have extended to the bottom, it would have helped mimicking the shape of the golden spiral. I wonder if changing ange would have allowed that.</td>', 'I like it. While the blown highlights certainly contribute to the ''sunny day'' feeling, a bit more detail in the leaves would have been pleasant. If the dark border on the left side would have extended to the bottom, it would have helped mimicking the shape of the golden spiral. I wonder if changing ange would have allowed that.', '2011-11-10 17:50:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591676, 983135, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting, more detail in the highlights (e.g. underexposing for the flowers) would have helped, I think. Composition is good.</td>', 'Interesting, more detail in the highlights (e.g. underexposing for the flowers) would have helped, I think. Composition is good.', '2011-11-10 17:52:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591678, 983156, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice idea. If there was wind, allowing for a slower shutter speed to blur the vegetation while keeping the subject sharp could have made for a different but still interesting image and enhance the feeling the boy is lost in his thoughts.</td>', 'Nice idea. If there was wind, allowing for a slower shutter speed to blur the vegetation while keeping the subject sharp could have made for a different but still interesting image and enhance the feeling the boy is lost in his thoughts.', '2011-11-10 17:57:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591694, 983076, 49018, '<td valign="top">Funny :) What about a reflector on the right side and/or a diffuser to soften the shadows a bit? Also, I wonder how a ''from the top'' angle would have worked.</td>', 'Funny :) What about a reflector on the right side and/or a diffuser to soften the shadows a bit? Also, I wonder how a ''from the top'' angle would have worked.', '2011-11-10 18:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591698, 982970, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice high key, I love the tone. The black point and dense shadows work well here because of the subject tones and complexion. The hint of square in the background works very well in leading to the subject, much better than a uniform background would have. Is this a very subtle tritone or pure grayscale?</td>', 'Nice high key, I love the tone. The black point and dense shadows work well here because of the subject tones and complexion. The hint of square in the background works very well in leading to the subject, much better than a uniform background would have. Is this a very subtle tritone or pure grayscale?', '2011-11-10 18:13:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591699, 983073, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice image. I feel a bit more fill light for the shadow and/or no blown highlights (particularly on the grapes, that shade of red whashes out quite easily when overexposing) would have improved the image. Also, I think the balance would be much better without the left arm in sight. Very nice light.</td>', 'Nice image. I feel a bit more fill light for the shadow and/or no blown highlights (particularly on the grapes, that shade of red whashes out quite easily when overexposing) would have improved the image. Also, I think the balance would be much better without the left arm in sight. Very nice light.', '2011-11-10 18:19:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591702, 983058, 49018, '<td valign="top">Good idea. I think more even perhaps frontal, lighting would have helped. Given the subject, being able to see more fine detail would be a considerable plus.</td>', 'Good idea. I think more even perhaps frontal, lighting would have helped. Given the subject, being able to see more fine detail would be a considerable plus.', '2011-11-10 18:24:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591714, 982325, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting. I wonder if removing the pegboxes and/or taking a frontal angle, rather than one fro the upper right, would have made for a better image. That particular kind of glossy, dark material in the egs and keyboard is always a bit tricky to manage and the loss of detail due to the shallow, but not quite, DOF  detracts  a bit from the image. Possibly, putting the pegboxes completely out of focus or focussing on these while blurring the rest would have worked. Or possibly a polarizer on lens or flash to kill the highlights while keeping contrast.(not sure if it works on laquired wood reflections, though..)</td>', 'Interesting. I wonder if removing the pegboxes and/or taking a frontal angle, rather than one fro the upper right, would have made for a better image. That particular kind of glossy, dark material in the egs and keyboard is always a bit tricky to manage and the loss of detail due to the shallow, but not quite, DOF  detracts  a bit from the image. Possibly, putting the pegboxes completely out of focus or focussing on these while blurring the rest would have worked. Or possibly a polarizer on lens or flash to kill the highlights while keeping contrast.(not sure if it works on laquired wood reflections, though..)', '2011-11-10 18:43:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591715, 983152, 49018, '<td valign="top">Lovely. I am curious to find out about how this was shot.</td>', 'Lovely. I am curious to find out about how this was shot.', '2011-11-10 18:45:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591719, 983072, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like very much the shade in the sky, it adds depth. I hate the lamps, along with cctv cams are really a bane for architectural shots. Very good image.</td>', 'I like very much the shade in the sky, it adds depth. I hate the lamps, along with cctv cams are really a bane for architectural shots. Very good image.', '2011-11-10 18:49:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591720, 982972, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like the ripples a lot. Much less the hard shadows. It is a pity that the kind of angled light that makes for an interesting water surface also makes for a very extreme range. Maybe a bit of extra fill in flash could have helped lifting the shadows while keeping more detail in the highlights?</td>', 'I like the ripples a lot. Much less the hard shadows. It is a pity that the kind of angled light that makes for an interesting water surface also makes for a very extreme range. Maybe a bit of extra fill in flash could have helped lifting the shadows while keeping more detail in the highlights?', '2011-11-10 18:56:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591722, 983147, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like the duotone here, it works well., as it does the very shallow DOF and the blown up highlights keeping the interest on eyes and moustaches. Good portrait.</td>', 'I like the duotone here, it works well., as it does the very shallow DOF and the blown up highlights keeping the interest on eyes and moustaches. Good portrait.', '2011-11-10 18:59:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591745, 983084, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice texture. Maybe having the background a bit out of focus would have helped creating separation. Thsi way it looks almost painted rather than three dimensional.</td>', 'Nice texture. Maybe having the background a bit out of focus would have helped creating separation. Thsi way it looks almost painted rather than three dimensional.', '2011-11-10 19:34:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591749, 983094, 49018, '<td valign="top">Not sure about this. While the three tones work well (very bright boats, very dark sea and midtone land/sky) the image lacks of definition and the framing is very static. I think cropping out most of the image left of the boat would give more the impression of directing home, particularly if the vassel was actually oriented more towards the shore. The blotchiness of the image is a bit of a let down. Challenge and basic editing aside, I think it would work better blurring the image and adding quite a lot of fake analog grain in photoshop or some other software.</td>', 'Not sure about this. While the three tones work well (very bright boats, very dark sea and midtone land/sky) the image lacks of definition and the framing is very static. I think cropping out most of the image left of the boat would give more the impression of directing home, particularly if the vassel was actually oriented more towards the shore. The blotchiness of the image is a bit of a let down. Challenge and basic editing aside, I think it would work better blurring the image and adding quite a lot of fake analog grain in photoshop or some other software.', '2011-11-10 19:42:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591750, 983104, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like it. I know that getting more depth of field with this kind of macro is pretty complicated, but having the tip of the right stem in focus would work better. Also, an angle or a choice of exposure minimizing the portion of overexposed sky in the left reflection would add a lot, in my opinion. However, probably it''s just me.</td>', 'I like it. I know that getting more depth of field with this kind of macro is pretty complicated, but having the tip of the right stem in focus would work better. Also, an angle or a choice of exposure minimizing the portion of overexposed sky in the left reflection would add a lot, in my opinion. However, probably it''s just me.', '2011-11-10 19:46:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591754, 982367, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice concept.</td>', 'Nice concept.', '2011-11-10 19:51:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591755, 982996, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very nice postprocessing</td>', 'Very nice postprocessing', '2011-11-10 19:53:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591758, 983129, 137570, '<td valign="top">It''s got something</td>', 'It''s got something', '2011-11-10 19:55:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591759, 982922, 137570, '<td valign="top">Great colors</td>', 'Great colors', '2011-11-10 19:57:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591760, 983104, 137570, '<td valign="top">Cool reflections! Nicely done.</td>', 'Cool reflections! Nicely done.', '2011-11-10 20:00:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591761, 983080, 137570, '<td valign="top">Very well done... That''s my winner!</td>', 'Very well done... That''s my winner!', '2011-11-10 20:04:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591762, 982972, 94265, '<td valign="top">A little bright on the highlights but the details are still there. Nice blues.</td>', 'A little bright on the highlights but the details are still there. Nice blues.', '2011-11-10 20:06:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591763, 983080, 94265, '<td valign="top">This made me chuckle, I''m sure I''ve seen something similar on DeviantArt before. Good idea.</td>', 'This made me chuckle, I''m sure I''ve seen something similar on DeviantArt before. Good idea.', '2011-11-10 20:07:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591764, 982183, 94265, '<td valign="top">I can''t see where the Golden Ratio fits any focal point in this shot but I love it all the same. Great sillhouette shot, love those bokeh lights.</td>', 'I can''t see where the Golden Ratio fits any focal point in this shot but I love it all the same. Great sillhouette shot, love those bokeh lights.', '2011-11-10 20:07:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591767, 983157, 49018, '<td valign="top">Not too keen on a subject, or lack thereof, maybe because it all appears a bit flat. But I do find the two patches of red attractive in the way they mirror each other. I think a bit of under exposure would have helped retaining detail in highlights and strenghtening colors, while keeping everything sharper. Also, maybe choosing a later or earlier time of the day would have given you a more dramatic light to play with. But that''s just my opinion, no offence taken I hope.</td>', 'Not too keen on a subject, or lack thereof, maybe because it all appears a bit flat. But I do find the two patches of red attractive in the way they mirror each other. I think a bit of under exposure would have helped retaining detail in highlights and strenghtening colors, while keeping everything sharper. Also, maybe choosing a later or earlier time of the day would have given you a more dramatic light to play with. But that''s just my opinion, no offence taken I hope.', '2011-11-10 20:10:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591771, 982965, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice perspective and use of repeating patterns, I wonder if having captured the approaching figures closer would have made for a stronger image. Also, I wonder if either cropping down to the base of the lamp or exclude the lamp post completely by moving a bit forward would have improved the photo. This way it cuts the frame in half without quite reinforcing the motiv of lamp posts stretching in the distance..</td>', 'Nice perspective and use of repeating patterns, I wonder if having captured the approaching figures closer would have made for a stronger image. Also, I wonder if either cropping down to the base of the lamp or exclude the lamp post completely by moving a bit forward would have improved the photo. This way it cuts the frame in half without quite reinforcing the motiv of lamp posts stretching in the distance..', '2011-11-10 20:18:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591781, 983089, 49018, '<td valign="top">Pleasant, good cropping and natural looking. Maybe trimming to exclude the bed post on the top left corner would help leading the eye to the subject. Trimming more on the right as well, but I am less sure. The detail in the air is a bit jagged (not that I would know how to improve that, details defintion in black hair always gives me nightmares :) Good portrait, quite personal.</td>', 'Pleasant, good cropping and natural looking. Maybe trimming to exclude the bed post on the top left corner would help leading the eye to the subject. Trimming more on the right as well, but I am less sure. The detail in the air is a bit jagged (not that I would know how to improve that, details defintion in black hair always gives me nightmares :) Good portrait, quite personal.', '2011-11-10 20:25:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591784, 982800, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like the stark contrast between dark and shadow. Much of the strenght of this image is in the detail, so a bit more shadow detail would have worked better for me, but it might be my monitor. A few drops of water on the lock would have added texture too, but probably it''s just me.</td>', 'I like the stark contrast between dark and shadow. Much of the strenght of this image is in the detail, so a bit more shadow detail would have worked better for me, but it might be my monitor. A few drops of water on the lock would have added texture too, but probably it''s just me.', '2011-11-10 20:29:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591789, 983122, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very busy, maybe a closer framing on 67 to 31, with the opponents in the background, would have given me a stronger sense of imminent confrontation and also made quite a good use of the golden ratio as a composing device. But I really know little about american football, is the defensive coordinator the player facing us or the guy in nike cap and hearphones?</td>', 'Very busy, maybe a closer framing on 67 to 31, with the opponents in the background, would have given me a stronger sense of imminent confrontation and also made quite a good use of the golden ratio as a composing device. But I really know little about american football, is the defensive coordinator the player facing us or the guy in nike cap and hearphones?', '2011-11-10 20:41:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591790, 983063, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very defined and nice, naturally bright eyes (no spot editing allowed it''s a great thing in this sense).</td>', 'Very defined and nice, naturally bright eyes (no spot editing allowed it''s a great thing in this sense).', '2011-11-10 20:43:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591792, 983062, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like the idea. I wonder if keeping the arm''s shadows and bow darker would have made for a stronger, more graphical image</td>', 'I like the idea. I wonder if keeping the arm''s shadows and bow darker would have made for a stronger, more graphical image', '2011-11-10 20:46:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591804, 982486, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like it, the black and white is very natural and analogic. I woud love to see the colour version of this. Maybe a very slight increase in contrast would be more to my taste, but then, it''s my taste.</td>', 'I like it, the black and white is very natural and analogic. I woud love to see the colour version of this. Maybe a very slight increase in contrast would be more to my taste, but then, it''s my taste.', '2011-11-10 21:01:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591806, 982843, 49018, '<td valign="top">The idea is interesting, the overexposure spoils it a bit and sharpness is midway between a more decided and pleasant out of focus or tack sharp, which I am guessing is either due to limits of the camera or simply to this being a tiny crop from a much wider image. Being closer to the animals would have helped, even if the crop and/or the long focal lens help compressing distances and enhancing the feeling of a tight pack. The range of the image is quite vast, no direct light shining on the flanks of the horses, which makes difficult to retain shadow details on the brown ones. However, this almost backlit lighting is often used when photographing horses, as ri light on horses hair works just great and dust and frontal lighting create diffraction, which works well with this kind of shot. Panning from a closer distance could work as well, if you wish to convey a sense of speed. I have seen the same ''odd one'' concept in a photo taken from an helicopter, which really worked great. Sorry for the longwinded comment. If you have a chance is definitely worth another try, you could get some great images.</td>', 'The idea is interesting, the overexposure spoils it a bit and sharpness is midway between a more decided and pleasant out of focus or tack sharp, which I am guessing is either due to limits of the camera or simply to this being a tiny crop from a much wider image. Being closer to the animals would have helped, even if the crop and/or the long focal lens help compressing distances and enhancing the feeling of a tight pack. The range of the image is quite vast, no direct light shining on the flanks of the horses, which makes difficult to retain shadow details on the brown ones. However, this almost backlit lighting is often used when photographing horses, as ri light on horses hair works just great and dust and frontal lighting create diffraction, which works well with this kind of shot. Panning from a closer distance could work as well, if you wish to convey a sense of speed. I have seen the same ''odd one'' concept in a photo taken from an helicopter, which really worked great. Sorry for the longwinded comment. If you have a chance is definitely worth another try, you could get some great images.', '2011-11-10 21:02:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591960, 983152, 86218, '<td valign="top">Great shot. Lighting must have been very good for this to stand out in the basic editing. Nice work</td>', 'Great shot. Lighting must have been very good for this to stand out in the basic editing. Nice work', '2011-11-10 23:01:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591965, 983081, 86218, '<td valign="top">Strangely this works. Like this very much. Blue choise from Don for sure</td>', 'Strangely this works. Like this very much. Blue choise from Don for sure', '2011-11-10 23:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6591969, 983112, 86218, '<td valign="top">This pose is just the cutest. Black on white - perfect Really works.</td>', 'This pose is just the cutest. Black on white - perfect Really works.', '2011-11-10 23:13:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592156, 982819, 49018, '<td valign="top">South Africa? Very interesting subject and composition. Being the image this good, I would have loved to see a bit more details on her dress, but it really is a small thing. Well done.</td>', 'South Africa? Very interesting subject and composition. Being the image this good, I would have loved to see a bit more details on her dress, but it really is a small thing. Well done.', '2011-11-11 05:08:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592157, 983037, 49018, '<td valign="top">My favourite in the spiralish staircases subset :) I am not quite sure what the thing (doll house?) on the rail is, but the umbrealla definetely works great and the hint of a person underneath it also conveys a sense of movement.I like the processing, it looks like handheld hdr but with good taste.</td>', 'My favourite in the spiralish staircases subset :) I am not quite sure what the thing (doll house?) on the rail is, but the umbrealla definetely works great and the hint of a person underneath it also conveys a sense of movement.I like the processing, it looks like handheld hdr but with good taste.', '2011-11-11 05:08:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592158, 983078, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very interesting, clever framing. At first I though of a koala on a brown background :) I never thought of using facial features and tight framing to create this kind of illusion. Also, there is even a third image hidden in it. Rare image. 9</td>', 'Very interesting, clever framing. At first I though of a koala on a brown background :) I never thought of using facial features and tight framing to create this kind of illusion. Also, there is even a third image hidden in it. Rare image. 9', '2011-11-11 05:08:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592159, 983133, 49018, '<td valign="top">A very used and abused shot, perhaps.There is probably no photographer who never attempted this. But also an excellent photo and very graphical. The use of the hyperfocal distance is spot on. The diffraction from shooting into the sun is really well controlled, as it is the glare. Easy to expose but also difficult to expose really well. The silhouette is just perfect (please, don''t tell me you spent 30 minutes waiting for the sun while cutting cardboard out.. just joking..). 9</td>', 'A very used and abused shot, perhaps.There is probably no photographer who never attempted this. But also an excellent photo and very graphical. The use of the hyperfocal distance is spot on. The diffraction from shooting into the sun is really well controlled, as it is the glare. Easy to expose but also difficult to expose really well. The silhouette is just perfect (please, don''t tell me you spent 30 minutes waiting for the sun while cutting cardboard out.. just joking..). 9', '2011-11-11 05:08:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592160, 982183, 49018, '<td valign="top">Excellent silhouette. The beak is just perfect and the background creates a very effective vignette around the subject. Is this a real bird? In any case, a very nice, evocative image.</td>', 'Excellent silhouette. The beak is just perfect and the background creates a very effective vignette around the subject. Is this a real bird? In any case, a very nice, evocative image.', '2011-11-11 05:09:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592161, 982501, 49018, '<td valign="top">Lovely.</td>', 'Lovely.', '2011-11-11 05:10:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592162, 982922, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very graceful indeed and the choice of background highlights/vignetting complement the subject very pleasantly. I suppose a framing such that the dark area in the background would mimic the golden spiral curve would have fitted the challenge even more (and in a very litteral, perhaps boring way, so probably a bad idea). Very pleasant bokeh. 8 from me.</td>', 'Very graceful indeed and the choice of background highlights/vignetting complement the subject very pleasantly. I suppose a framing such that the dark area in the background would mimic the golden spiral curve would have fitted the challenge even more (and in a very litteral, perhaps boring way, so probably a bad idea). Very pleasant bokeh. 8 from me.', '2011-11-11 05:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592163, 983143, 49018, '<td valign="top">I like concept and result. I find the stronger shadow cast by the mask to make the photo somewhat unbalanced (but that just me, really). I wonder how it might look like with a refector lifting the shadow of the shell completely or even with a lighting setup so that the shell''s shadow projects upward. That would make for an interesting oblique symmetry. But that''s just me overthinking, good concept, well done!</td>', 'I like concept and result. I find the stronger shadow cast by the mask to make the photo somewhat unbalanced (but that just me, really). I wonder how it might look like with a refector lifting the shadow of the shell completely or even with a lighting setup so that the shell''s shadow projects upward. That would make for an interesting oblique symmetry. But that''s just me overthinking, good concept, well done!', '2011-11-11 05:11:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592164, 983079, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very well done. I am a bit unsure about the perhaps weak fill light and the background, as the head and hair might benefit from more separation fro the background. Maybe a second flash putting an highlight on the background could have helped (and a third one on the background behind the right foot to create a triangular motive mimicking the figure.. just, given I can barely switch a strobe on, probably I am just being delirious). Well done but, honestly, I find that turning this one in portrait orientation turns it from good to smashing excellent and so much more dynamic, with the body pulling away from light. Also, the lack of fill light from below, in vertical framing turns into a massive asset as the flower is anyway well lit.</td>', 'Very well done. I am a bit unsure about the perhaps weak fill light and the background, as the head and hair might benefit from more separation fro the background. Maybe a second flash putting an highlight on the background could have helped (and a third one on the background behind the right foot to create a triangular motive mimicking the figure.. just, given I can barely switch a strobe on, probably I am just being delirious). Well done but, honestly, I find that turning this one in portrait orientation turns it from good to smashing excellent and so much more dynamic, with the body pulling away from light. Also, the lack of fill light from below, in vertical framing turns into a massive asset as the flower is anyway well lit.', '2011-11-11 05:15:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592165, 982634, 49018, '<td valign="top">Lovely texture, choice of angle, exposure and of course time of the day. While it does not suggest me any particular feeling, I find it a very strong image, visually.</td>', 'Lovely texture, choice of angle, exposure and of course time of the day. While it does not suggest me any particular feeling, I find it a very strong image, visually.', '2011-11-11 05:15:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592168, 983123, 49018, '<td valign="top">Nice high key.</td>', 'Nice high key.', '2011-11-11 05:16:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592169, 983081, 49018, '<td valign="top">Is it just me or there are a ghostly face and the figure of a ghostly little girl lingering in the water? Very well captured and certainly a good use of the ratio.</td>', 'Is it just me or there are a ghostly face and the figure of a ghostly little girl lingering in the water? Very well captured and certainly a good use of the ratio.', '2011-11-11 05:19:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592170, 982678, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very suggestive. If there is one thing, a slightly longer focal lens might have compressed things a bit, this way the finger looks a bit distant from the face, as it belonged to someone else. But maybe that was the intention. I wonder how it would look if you were looking at the viewer. I really like your vision in this and other of your photographs.</td>', 'Very suggestive. If there is one thing, a slightly longer focal lens might have compressed things a bit, this way the finger looks a bit distant from the face, as it belonged to someone else. But maybe that was the intention. I wonder how it would look if you were looking at the viewer. I really like your vision in this and other of your photographs.', '2011-11-11 05:21:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592171, 983111, 49018, '<td valign="top">Quite cryptic image, and suggestive. I see a man figure in it, some arctic explorer (or possibly I am just tired).</td>', 'Quite cryptic image, and suggestive. I see a man figure in it, some arctic explorer (or possibly I am just tired).', '2011-11-11 05:21:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592172, 983151, 49018, '<td valign="top">I find the reflection and perspective extremely effective, creating the illusion of a much higher bridge when half of it is, well, reflection :) Very effective black and white and choice of angle.</td>', 'I find the reflection and perspective extremely effective, creating the illusion of a much higher bridge when half of it is, well, reflection :) Very effective black and white and choice of angle.', '2011-11-11 05:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592173, 982356, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very suggestive.</td>', 'Very suggestive.', '2011-11-11 05:23:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592179, 983061, 49018, '<td valign="top">I feel the hue (duotone?) works very well here.</td>', 'I feel the hue (duotone?) works very well here.', '2011-11-11 05:30:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592182, 983039, 49018, '<td valign="top">Interesting image, I like the hute shape and the smoky dust which makes for a more dynamic scene. I wonder whether it would have worked better cropping off completely the wall on the left and/or the area under the bridge. Even if the road sign gives some context and the two walls symmetry. I like the processing and texture, it works well for the whole image but for the left wall (sorry, I am taking it on the left wall :)</td>', 'Interesting image, I like the hute shape and the smoky dust which makes for a more dynamic scene. I wonder whether it would have worked better cropping off completely the wall on the left and/or the area under the bridge. Even if the road sign gives some context and the two walls symmetry. I like the processing and texture, it works well for the whole image but for the left wall (sorry, I am taking it on the left wall :)', '2011-11-11 05:48:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592355, 982972, 110041, '<td valign="top">Love the colours, the smoothness and crispness of the shot. However, i don''t think the ''Golden Ratio'' has worked particularly well in this crop.</td>', 'Love the colours, the smoothness and crispness of the shot. However, i don''t think the ''Golden Ratio'' has worked particularly well in this crop.', '2011-11-11 12:21:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592361, 982965, 110041, '<td valign="top">Good use of the ''Golden Ratio'' and good control of the DoF. Nice leading line of the railings leads the viewer to the people in the distance. My only wish would be for the people to be closer so you get an understanding of what they''re doing. That would make the shot that bit more interesting.</td>', 'Good use of the ''Golden Ratio'' and good control of the DoF. Nice leading line of the railings leads the viewer to the people in the distance. My only wish would be for the people to be closer so you get an understanding of what they''re doing. That would make the shot that bit more interesting.', '2011-11-11 12:25:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592363, 982584, 110041, '<td valign="top">The tower is by far the most interesting element of the shot. The ramp leads you in and makes you want to peer through the window. The problem with this crop is that you can''t see anything through the tower window and the rest of the photo is not interesting enough to compensate.</td>', 'The tower is by far the most interesting element of the shot. The ramp leads you in and makes you want to peer through the window. The problem with this crop is that you can''t see anything through the tower window and the rest of the photo is not interesting enough to compensate.', '2011-11-11 12:28:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592365, 983099, 110041, '<td valign="top">Love the textures. Crop works well.</td>', 'Love the textures. Crop works well.', '2011-11-11 12:28:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592369, 983132, 110041, '<td valign="top">Interesting. Don''t know what to make of this. I like the tones and the form is quite unusual. Not sure if the seemingly more in focus portion is a distraction. Good on you for going for something more abstract.</td>', 'Interesting. Don''t know what to make of this. I like the tones and the form is quite unusual. Not sure if the seemingly more in focus portion is a distraction. Good on you for going for something more abstract.', '2011-11-11 12:31:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592371, 982356, 110041, '<td valign="top">Creepy, mostly because you can make out that it''s a person. If it weren''t for the eye i''d probably like it more.</td>', 'Creepy, mostly because you can make out that it''s a person. If it weren''t for the eye i''d probably like it more.', '2011-11-11 12:33:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592374, 982932, 110041, '<td valign="top">He has no legs. :(<br/> <br/>I''d perhaps crop tighter to his head. I think his butt is actually quite distracting (probably evolved that way)</td>', 'He has no legs. :( I''d perhaps crop tighter to his head. I think his butt is actually quite distracting (probably evolved that way)', '2011-11-11 12:35:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592376, 983062, 110041, '<td valign="top">Could do with being levelled off.</td>', 'Could do with being levelled off.', '2011-11-11 12:37:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592821, 982183, 17153, '<td valign="top">beautiful silhouette and background - i just wish you''ve cropped the left a bit more! bumping up to 8</td>', 'beautiful silhouette and background - i just wish you''ve cropped the left a bit more! bumping up to 8', '2011-11-12 08:07:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592853, 982988, 94265, '<td valign="top">Wish we were a little closer to the bird. Love those blues.</td>', 'Wish we were a little closer to the bird. Love those blues.', '2011-11-12 10:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592854, 982959, 94265, '<td valign="top">I adore Plovers, they''re just lovely. Nice shot, the red trim around its eye really stands out.</td>', 'I adore Plovers, they''re just lovely. Nice shot, the red trim around its eye really stands out.', '2011-11-12 10:24:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6592912, 983080, 25190, '<td valign="top">Very creative in the challenge good composition nice and sharp ..Congrats well thought image</td>', 'Very creative in the challenge good composition nice and sharp ..Congrats well thought image', '2011-11-12 12:48:35.000000', NULL, 1),
